' Lab 3 · Task 3 · Scenario 3 — Session Verification & Token Rotation
' Unified human actor "User"; context role shown via note.
' Session storage & refresh-token rotation per lab3/adr/0007-sessions-storage.md.

@startuml
title SchemaPostol - Scenario 3: Session Verification & Token Rotation (03-token-refresh)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

' ---------- Unified human actor + system + DB entities ----------
actor "User" as HumanUser
participant "Frontend" as FE
participant "Backend" as BE
database "User" as UserEntity
database "Session" as SessionEntity

note right of HumanUser
  Unified actor **User**.
  Context role: **Registered User** while the session is valid,
  degrades to **Guest** when the refresh token is rejected.
end note

'
' ================= SESSION VERIFICATION =================
'
== Authorized request ==

HumanUser -> FE : perform an authorized action
activate FE
FE -> BE : GET /api/schematics (Bearer accessToken)
activate BE
BE -> BE : verifyJwt(accessToken)
alt accessToken valid
  BE --> FE : 200 OK - requested operation executed
else accessToken invalid / expired
  BE --> FE : 401 Unauthorized {error: "refresh token required"}
end
deactivate BE

'
' ================= TOKEN ROTATION =================
'
opt access token was rejected - refresh flow
  FE -> BE : POST /auth/refresh\n(HttpOnly refreshToken cookie attached by browser)
  activate BE
  BE -> SessionEntity : findByHash(hash(refreshToken)) + check expires_at
  activate SessionEntity
  SessionEntity --> BE : session | null
  deactivate SessionEntity
  alt refreshToken valid (session exists, not expired)
    BE -> BE : rotate - generate new accessToken + refreshToken
    BE -> SessionEntity : updateSession(session_id,\nhash(newRefreshToken))
    activate SessionEntity
    SessionEntity --> BE : OK
    deactivate SessionEntity
    BE --> FE : 200 OK - new accessToken (json) +\nnew refreshToken (HttpOnly cookie)
  else refreshToken invalid / expired / stolen
    BE -> SessionEntity : deleteSession(session_id)
    activate SessionEntity
    SessionEntity --> BE : OK
    deactivate SessionEntity
    BE --> FE : 401 Unauthorized - clear refreshToken cookie
  end
  deactivate BE
  note over FE
    **Token storage:** the new `accessToken` is kept in JS memory;
    the browser manages the refreshed HttpOnly cookie.
    On failure tokens are cleared and **User becomes Guest**.
  end note
end
deactivate FE

note over SessionEntity
  **Session (ADR-0007):** refresh token is stored HASHED; rotation
  happens on every `POST /auth/refresh`, enabling theft detection
  and instant revocation by `user_id`.
end note

@enduml